            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CMINNER"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I thought this marinade was flavorful and made the meat tender. I used canola oil instead of grapeseed, yellow mustard instead of ground mustard (because I didn't have any) and no bay leaves. I loved the marinade but I think next time, I'll cut the oil in half...it just seemed to be too much. Great recipe- no steak sauce needed on the side!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Massey"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Super easy &amp; I had all the ingredients! I used it for cubed roast in the crockpot. I cooked it in the marinade on low for 4 hours. Everyone loved it! The meat just fell apart. It was great with rice, quinoa, and in tacos!",
            "datePublished": "2017-01-25T12:25:14.380Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "dparsell"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious, tender steak! Used this marinade for on London broil for our 4th of July BBQ. Many compliments and requests for the recipe. I follow it as written except that I didn't have dry mustard so I used a packet mustard. Marinaded over night. Then grilled. Came out great",
            "datePublished": "2017-07-07T01:38:56.163Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Joanne"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Absolutely Delicious! I used about 5 lbs chuck steak that comes 3 to a pack. Because I never think a day ahead, I grilled one of the steaks after about 6 hrs. The aroma was wonderful! We could only imagine how the other 2 would be after marinating overnight! We grilled them for brunch, and OMG! The steak was tender,juicy and so flavorful! I thin the liquid smoke helps, so don't leave it out! I varied a tad from the recipe, because I didn't have grape seed oil, I used olive oil. I also ran low on Worcestershire sauce so only had little over 1/4c and lastly I used a whole lime, otherwise would have had to find another recipe to use up the rest of it. I am adding this to my recipe box and will use it over and over! Thanks!",
            "datePublished": "2011-05-16T13:08:28.620Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kim Davidson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Awesome! I substituted canola oil for the grapeseed and left out the bay leaves ('cuz I didn't have any). The batch made just the right amount for 5 pounds of London Broil. My kids LOVED it and so did I!",
            "datePublished": "2010-05-26T21:25:16.013Z"
